      "narrative": {
        "summary_notes": "The Targeted Case Manager (TCM) received and reviewed a Case Manager's Referral for a newly assigned case for services. After reviewing the referral with the supervisor, the TCM signed the referral form and began collecting all necessary information required for the admission process. Following this review, the TCM accepted Esneldo Gomez Gomez's case for Targeted Case Management services. The TCM successfully contacted Esneldo by phone and introduced himself as a Targeted Case Manager from ARC Mental Health. The purpose of the call and the receipt of a referral for Targeted Case Management services were explained. The TCM verified whether Esneldo was currently receiving Targeted Case Management services from another agency, which he denied. Esneldo reported ongoing symptoms associated with major depressive disorder, generalized anxiety disorder, and insomnia, including depressed mood, worry, nervousness, and difficulty sleeping, and he stated that these symptoms affected his emotional stability and daily functioning despite current treatment. Esneldo reported that he was doing well with his medications and indicated a continued need for support with coordination of behavioral health and medical care, follow-up appointments, medication management oversight, transportation planning, and assistance navigating healthcare-related responsibilities. Esneldo described that uninterrupted access to psychiatric and medical care was important to maintain symptom stability, preserve medication adherence, and reduce risk of worsening depression, anxiety, and sleep disturbance. In response, the TCM requested his address in order to coordinate an in-person visit. Later that day, the TCM conducted a face-to-face visit at Esneldo's residence to assess his needs, strengths, and barriers and to initiate the admission and evaluation process. Esneldo was cooperative, communicative, and receptive throughout the visit."
